Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  Judith A Ferry  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Tracy L  Davis  M D  Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Abner Louissaint  M D   Ph D  Reports To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  57 year old woman with excisional biopsy for microcalcifications associated with intraductal carcinoma and DCIS on biopsy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL  456   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA WITH MIXED LOBULAR AND DUCTAL FEATURES  IN SITU CARCINOMA OF AMBIGUOUS TYPE  WITH COMEDONECROSIS AND CALCIFICATIONS  SEE TABLE AND NOTE  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Both the in situ and invasive carcinoma show ambiguous features with respect to ductal or lobular subtype  The architectural pattern of the invasive carcinoma in this sample favors lobular carcinoma  however  an immunohistochemical stain for E cadherin shows moderate cytoplasmic positivity with focal membrane accentuation  The in situ carcinoma has a predominantly solid architectural pattern with rare microacini  cellular dishesion  and areas of comedonecrosis and calcification  E cadherin staining is variable within the in situ component  from negative staining to moderate positivity with membrane accentuation  In view of the ambiguous features of the in situ carcinoma in this specimen  it would be prudent to treat it as DCIS with respect to margins on this specimen  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  Several microscopic foci  spanning from   0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  GRADE  1 LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma focally extends to   0 05cm from the anterior and superior margins  IN SITU CARCINOMA  Within and beyond the invasive foci  MARGINS OF IN SITU CARCINOMA  In situ carcinoma is present   0 2cm from multiple margins  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  NONSENTINEL  EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left sentinel node  456   is a 1 4 cm rubbery tan lymph node with attached yellow red fat  The node is dissected from the fat  bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the specimen is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0 cm oriented breast tissue with a needle localization wire placed  with short stitch designating superior and long designating lateral  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior is blue  posterior is black  superior is green  and inferior is yellow  Serial sectioning  from medial to lateral  revealed a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0 cm biopsy cavity  located 2 1cm from the medial end  5 2cm from the lateral end  0 4cm from the inferior margin  0 1cm from the superior margin  0 4cm from the posterior margin and 0 4cm from the anterior margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section between medial end and biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section around biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections corresponding to subsequent tissue sections  including slice marked by localization wire   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of tissue around biopsy cavity and area indicated by localization wire   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end  Note  Essentially the entire biopsy site and the region bracketed by the wires corresponding to the region of interest have been submitted  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  non sentinel tissue   are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue  measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm  Five potential lymph nodes are identified in this tissue  Four potential lymph nodes are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One large lymph node is serially sectioned and submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT SENTINEL  456   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Gross Dictation by Abner Louissaint M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Abner Louissaint M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Abner Louissaint M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administr