 the mass appears atrophic  This case also was reviewed at an MGH breast  pathology division conference on REMOVED_DATE     The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone  receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ  hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  will be  reported in an addendum     BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR FLAP   EXCISION   UNREMARKABLE FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY     LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   EXCISION   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO OF TWO NODES  0 2   SEE NOTE   THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED     NOTE  To evaluate for metastatic carcinoma  immunohistochemical stains for  cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin were examined on levels  from each of three blocks  The findings support the above diagnosis     GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received are 3 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN     Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right axillary sentinel  node   are 2 lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm   respectively  The smaller lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1   now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The larger lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1A  now  as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining fibroadipose tissue is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 2cm  mastectomy  specimen with a suture designating the 12 o clock position  A REMOVED_DATE x 10 5cm   ellipse of skin overlies a round  fluctuant mass in the upper outer quadrant   externally measuring 10cm in greatest dimension and spanning from the 7  o clock to 11 o clock position  and extending from the lateral aspect of the  areolus to 11 5cm from the nipple  A 0 4cm  well healed scar overl